  "meta": {
    "space": "embeddings_ability.npy",
    "projection": "classical MDS + SMACOF, canonically oriented",
    "clustering": "average-linkage agglomerative on cosine distance, 2 levels",
    "cards": 88,
    "unresolved": [],
    "note": "Positions are LOCAL to this deck and are not atlas positions — the deck is re-laid-out from its own cards, which is the whole point. Anything that draws this must say so.",
    "named_by": "deck-cartographer",
    "cartographer_notes": [
      "The whole rules-verified record is four cards — Hapatra, Mikaeus, Ashnod's Altar and Blood Artist, the board of passing stack 001 — and they sit in three different regions: THE MINT, DRAIN AND REBUY (two of them) and THE FREE OUTLETS. The engine is an axis across the map, not a city. Worth saying out loud that stack 001 is a REFUTATION: it proved the Mikaeus-plus-altar pairings return once and stop, so those verified marks record what does not loop.",
      "The mass is in the wrong half for the deck's own story, and the map shows it cleanly. THE BUSINESS END holds 26 of 88 entries, all payoff; THE COUNTER SUPPLY holds nine, and one of those nine places no counters. Nine sources feed twenty-six payoffs, which is the same asymmetry strategic_frame states as 'Hapatra is a mint, not a source'.",
      "city-4-hood-1 groups Blowfly Infestation and Necroskitter — both of which trigger on a creature dying with a -1/-1 counter on it — with Toxic Deluge, which places no counters at all (it is -X/-X). Deluge is the misfit of the map: it mints no Snakes and turns on neither of its neighbours. The membership is defensible (all three are mass/dies-based black removal) but the hood's real job belongs to the other two, which is what the gloss says.",
      "city-3 and city-5 each have exactly one neighbourhood whose membership is identical to the city's. There is no split to name, so both are left to the deterministic word rather than given a synonym of their parent.",
      "Lazotep Quarry is filed in LANDS THAT DO MORE, but stack 001's outlet census counts it as one of the deck's eight mana-free sacrifice outlets. Anyone reading THE FREE OUTLETS as the complete list will count seven; the real number is eight, and the eighth is a land.",
      "Ashnod's Altar and Phyrexian Altar are mana-producing artifacts and the space filed them with the sacrifice outlets, not with BORROWED SPEED. That is the ability space getting it right: their job is eating creatures, and the mana is the by-product.",
      "Orcish Bowmasters in DEATHS INTO CARDS is the softest membership on the map — it draws you nothing and punishes opponents' draws instead. It keys off drawing, so the neighbourhood is not wrong, but it is the one card there that does not refill your hand.",
      "Svogthos, the Restless Tomb has no entry in card_roles.json (deck-facts flags it), so it contributed nothing to its own placement. It landed in THE HOME COLOURS with the basics and the dual, which is where a B/G manland belongs anyway."
    ]
  },
